Ben Jonson, played by Sebastian Armesto.

10
01:12:13,333 --> 01:12:19,333
Anonymous is a 2011 period drama film directed by
Roland Emmerich and written by John Orloff.

11
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
The film is a fictionalized version of the life of Edward de Vere, 17th Earl of Oxford, an Elizabethan courtier,
playwright, poet and patron of the arts, and suggests he was the actual author of William Shakespeare's plays.

12
01:26:40,000 --> 01:26:46,000
It stars Rhys Ifans as de Vere and Vanessa Redgrave
as Queen Elizabeth I of England.

13
01:33:53,333 --> 01:33:59,333
The film premiered at the Toronto International
Film Festival on September 11, 2011.

14
01:41:06,666 --> 01:41:12,666
Produced by Centropolis Entertainment and Studio Babelsberg and distributed by Columbia Pictures, Anonymous was released on October 28,
2011 in the United States, Canada and the United Kingdom, expanding to theatres around the world in the following weeks.

15
01:48:20,000 --> 01:48:26,000
The film performed poorly at the box office and received mixed reviews from critics for praising its performances and visual achievements, but
criticising the film's time-jumping format, factual errors, and promotion of the Oxfordian theory of Shakespeare authorship.

